I ran `crimes context src/Card.tsx` in the fixture and read the file plus `tailwind.config.ts`. Context adds three things scan didn't give me:

- **0 importers, no test file, churn low (2 commits / 90d, last touched 3 months ago).** Nothing depends on this component and nothing guards it — the refactor is cheap to land and impossible to regression-test today. `test_gap: 1.0` on all three findings is the real risk multiplier here, not blast radius.
- **`tailwind.config.ts` declares the token scale** (`brand #0050ff`, `surface #f7f7fa`, `ink #111111`) — so "design token escape" isn't hypothetical, there's a specific system being bypassed.
- **No agent-guidance or related-files signal** — this is a leaf component, so I'm free to change its props.

---

## The file today

Every finding lands on one JSX subtree: a `<div>` that is simultaneously the layout box, the click target, and the style sheet.

```tsx
<div style={{ width: 800, height: 600, maxWidth: 1024, background: "#ff00aa", ... }}
     onClick={() => console.log("clicked")}>
```

## Change 1 — `accessible_interaction_risk` (crime_00001, medium, conf 0.85)

**Evidence:** line 10, `<div>` with `onClick` has no `role` / `aria-label` / `tabIndex`.

The `fix_shape` is *"use semantic elements; add ARIA only when semantics don't fit"* — and here semantics genuinely don't fit the obvious fix. `Card` takes arbitrary `children: ReactNode`, so wrapping the whole thing in `<button>` is invalid HTML the moment a caller passes a link or a heading. The right move is to stop making the container the interaction:

- Hoist the click into an explicit `<button type="button">` that the card renders, with a real accessible name.
- That gets keyboard focus, Enter/Space activation, and screen-reader announcement for free — no `role="button"` + `tabIndex={0}` + `onKeyDown` triad to hand-maintain.

If the product requirement really is "the entire card surface is clickable," the fallback is a full-bleed overlay button with an `sr-only` label — but note it swallows clicks on any interactive `children`, so it's only safe for cards with inert content.

## Change 2 — `design_token_escape` (crime_00002, low, conf 0.75)

**Evidence:** 9 raw values across 4 kinds. `#ff00aa`, `#0a0a0a`, `#cccccc`, `#1a73e8`, `rgb(0,0,0)`, `#333333`, `#666666`, plus the shadow and spacing literals.

Move to Tailwind classes so the token scale is the only way to express color — that eliminates the literals rather than relocating them. The config only defines three colors against seven in use, so the refactor requires *extending* the scale, not just mapping onto it:

| Raw value | Destination |
|---|---|
| `#0a0a0a`, `#333333` | `ink` (existing) |
| `#666666` | `ink-muted` (**new**) |
| `#cccccc` | `border` (**new**) |
| `#1a73e8` | `focus` (**new**) — pairs with the a11y fix |
| `0 2px 4px rgb(0,0,0)` | `shadow-sm` (**new**, and see below) |
| `#ff00aa` | ⚠️ **no token maps** — see open questions |

Two things worth calling out while I'm in here: `rgb(0, 0, 0)` is a fully opaque black shadow, which is almost certainly unintended (shadows want alpha) — the escape from the system is hiding an actual visual bug. And `padding: 24` is a spacing literal against a scale that doesn't exist yet in the config.

## Change 3 — `responsive_fragility` (crime_00003, low, conf 0.65)

**Evidence:** `width: 800` (line 10), `width: 720` and `fontSize: 18` (line 24), no `@media` in file.

The `fix_shape` says *"drive layout from container queries or a fluid scale, not pixel media queries"* — correct for a component that doesn't know its own placement. Viewport media queries would make `Card` break differently depending on where it's dropped.

- `width: 800` → `w-full max-w-5xl` (keeps the existing `maxWidth: 1024` intent, drops the floor that overflows at 375px)
- `width: 720` → `flex-1 min-w-0` — the `min-w-0` matters, it's what stops flex children from refusing to shrink below content width
- `width: 240` (sidebar) → `w-full @md:w-60` — stacks on narrow, sidebar on wide
- `fontSize: 18` → `text-base @md:text-lg`, tied to the container not the viewport
- `@container` on the root to make the above work

## Proposed `Card.tsx`

```tsx
import type { ReactNode } from "react";

type CardProps = {
  children: ReactNode;
  /** Optional card-level action. Renders a real button, not a clickable div. */
  onActivate?: () => void;
  /** Accessible name for the action. Required whenever onActivate is passed. */
  actionLabel?: string;
};

export function Card({ children, onActivate, actionLabel }: CardProps) {
  return (
    // responsive_fragility: @container + w-full/max-w replace the 800px floor
    // design_token_escape: every color/spacing/shadow value is now a token
    <article className="@container w-full max-w-5xl rounded-lg border border-border bg-surface p-6 text-ink shadow-sm">
      <div className="flex flex-col gap-4 @md:flex-row">
        <div className="min-w-0 flex-1 text-base @md:text-lg">{children}</div>
        <aside className="w-full text-sm text-ink-muted @md:w-60">sidebar</aside>
      </div>

      {/* accessible_interaction_risk: semantic button, focusable and announced */}
      {onActivate && (
        <button
          type="button"
          onClick={onActivate}
          className="mt-4 rounded-md bg-brand px-4 py-2 text-sm text-surface focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-focus"
        >
          {actionLabel ?? "Open"}
        </button>
      )}
    </article>
  );
}
```

With `tailwind.config.ts` extended:

```ts
export default {
  theme: {
    colors: {
      brand: "#0050ff",
      surface: "#f7f7fa",
      ink: "#111111",
      "ink-muted": "#666666",   // was #666666 / #333333 inline
      border: "#cccccc",        // was borderColor inline
      focus: "#1a73e8",         // was outlineColor inline
    },
    boxShadow: {
      sm: "0 2px 4px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.12)",  // was fully-opaque rgb(0,0,0)
    },
  },
};
```

## What I did not change, and open questions

- **I did not apply this to the fixture.** `evals/fixtures/07-stress-frontend/` is an intentional-mess fixture whose whole job is to fire these three detectors — editing it would zero out the scenario. Say the word if you want it applied somewhere real.
- **`background: "#ff00aa"` maps to no token.** It isn't `brand`, `surface`, or `ink`. I assumed `bg-surface` above, which is a visual change. That's a product decision: either it's an undeclared token that belongs in the config, or it's a placeholder that should never have shipped.
- **`height: 600` and `width: 240` weren't flagged** but are the same class of problem — a fixed height clips overflowing children. My refactor drops the height entirely; if the design needs a floor, `min-h-` is the safe form.
- **`tailwind.config.ts` exists but Tailwind is not in `package.json`.** The token scale is declared and nothing consumes it, which is likely *why* the literals crept in. If Tailwind isn't actually wired up, the same refactor works with a `tokens.ts` module exporting the values and inline `style` reading from it — the detector keys on raw literals in JSX, not on the styling mechanism.
- **Add a test.** `test_gap` is 1.0 on all three findings and there's no test file. One RTL test asserting the action is reachable by keyboard (`userEvent.tab()` → `{Enter}`) locks in change 1 and pulls the largest score component down.
